{"title":"Best fiction of 2025","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/927828965/0/marginalrevolution~Best-fiction-of.html","date":1763280287000,"content":"<p>Solvej Balle, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Calculation-Book-II-Solvej-Balle/dp/0811237273/ref=tmm_pap_swatch_0\" target=\"_blank\">On the Calculation of Volume I, Volume II</a>.  Volume III is due out in English late this year I have read it already in German.  A very strong series, reading ahead in German is a good demonstration of how much I like them.</p>\r\n<p>Suat Dervis, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Prisoner-Ankara-Novel-Suat-Dervis/dp/189274693X/ref=sr_1_1?crid=3A9UQYFJKMWHC&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.tRhvakDIaj2HQy0VFV-OFk5wcVQu_MsQGn7EaaIjfUS-j6kWyaefYox5n7c3zZSoBffWHiwdXSCTkMQ6WwxXqlgaoIpZHBLPqVwnJzIGWP8.F4qRTKnw3nFvTGkM3ZR7AAdwtMl2ogXvr6RKRUI9qJ4&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=prisoner+of+ankara&amp;qid=1763077802&amp;sprefix=prisoner+of+ankara%2Caps%2C308&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">The Prisoner of Ankara</a>.  A Turkish novel from mid-century, in English for the first time.</p>\r\n<p>Emmanuel Carrere, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/V13-Chronicle-Trial-Emmanuel-Carr%C3%A8re/dp/0374615705/ref=sr_1_1?crid=3948W0GDCCIY9&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.huXCi8js5TDxe8bKbE6pTA.wgGt0Tu2rQQngyv4Jy_oBV9biYfsZCduHDcYISPMAJU&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=V13%3A+Chronicle+of+a+Trial&amp;qid=1763077836&amp;sprefix=v13+chronicle+of+a+trial%2Caps%2C311&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">V13: Chronicle of a Trial</a>.  Non-fiction but it is more likely reading fiction, it just happens to be true (supposedly).</p>\r\n<p>Alain Mabanckou, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Dealing-Dead-Alain-Mabanckou/dp/1800817703/ref=sr_1_1?crid=8AHZF2K5FK43&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.t90tpqDFoG6Ym8ZC8svA-Tyc1m7Qx-KBd1uIt7A17RSwhklyhzR5mLf5uFo8bRnWJUtZkduRTq1Vcbvj9zgXSHymw5m18B7ZR63ZLM-aKWgMNI_W-MAL-aLlMw94R78SSOEzG7bzmk9QeAPOnEUVjCLH2gu6trtkigVEssbI569JpY9trcJmeHXfztsBI4G6OEy05h_2aBYqTuvBjl4ay-Opw3XYLmpYbuMe1ZLGgFo.2HBgE_8J8q5ElRWjapz_IFxJyATZA-LEq_UVHUO8UqU&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Dealing+with+the+Dead&amp;qid=1740611764&amp;sprefix=dealing+with+the+dead%2Caps%2C68&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Dealing with the Dead</a>.  Most African fiction does not connect with me, and there is a tendency for the reviews to be untrustworthy.  This “cemetery memoir,” from the Congo (via UCLA), held my interest throughout.</p>\r\n<p>Kiran Desai, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/10/the-loneliness-of-sonia-and-sunny-now-finished.html\" target=\"_blank\">The Loneliness of Sonia and Sunny</a>.</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/E%C3%A7a_de_Queiroz\" target=\"_blank\">Eça de Queiros</a>, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Adam-Eve-Paradise-E%C3%A7a-Queir%C3%B3s/dp/0811239144/ref=sr_1_1?crid=2SRNFP4QUFKWA&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.yIRo6NFdPE62enBR9vhTq92yORv79H9zk1LEHdDRdVJpsWkILHnBQDfowSosq3RMECpiifSvVGDsoAVWJA_8JE0SDY1nblMd08_ar49Gjyg5bs-EwS5jPfWl5H21jekbOxN4sv1xHUSxFqE3O6mMpVNKyIK_iX6-GjPIm_iaik_ra8TuSXSEscyIsR58Zr4FasL5zbqEh50Q9O-6CrZ1ndi3JXqBaWdJAjug2AJ2-dY.VMF06zJl0OvyxFpBtwcetDVqq8cPcj_qRzjLx_Oxg18&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=adam+and+eve+in+paradise+book&amp;qid=1763077970&amp;sprefix=adam+and+eve+in+para%2Caps%2C485&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Adam and Eve in Paradise</a>.  Originally from the 19th century, but translated into English only this year. A 60 pp. novella about exactly what the title indicates, noting that matters are not as simple as the first telling of that story might have suggested.</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Poems-Seamus-Heaney/dp/0374235236/ref=sr_1_1?crid=1M3NGY6HK90XD&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.BfkikyrpcPX8MClNC_KPeYglVOQGUppydom6FtgdgfjazC5t9uEN6dGJJTRS21rNXfNoU5ottsmRvtwHvG5gN9yW9luuqrIhRf1NbvQPQcvb4dX6n_Yym2h3J0jIx552Vflmwsh6PNZw_IylCzmHb8GD04BaMNJi2WARj3Y06PcNApWWyhITj11_BCENaJDf9bju45CFVk1B92fGV_gE2E0zjMgD_7bX-C1-41c_l4c.nYpvlhvs8GP8hxkzoNj6nXtgAdbeI-0kH2X87J5AhTk&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=poems+of+seamus+heaney&amp;qid=1763077601&amp;sprefix=poems+of+sea%2Caps%2C319&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">The Poems of Seamus Heaney</a>.  Not yet received, but obviously this is a winner.</p>\r\n<p>Overall, the Balle, Desai, and Heaney make for very strong entries, so this was a good year for fiction.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/11/best-fiction-of-2025.html\">Best fiction of 2025</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/927828965/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/927828965/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/927828965/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/927828965/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/927828965/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/email20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/20/927828965/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/rss20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/11/best-fiction-of-2025.html#respond\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/comments20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/11/best-fiction-of-2025.html/feed\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/commentsrss20.png\" /></a><h3>Related Stories</h3><ul><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/11/the-science-of-second-chances.html?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=the-science-of-second-chances\">*The Science of Second Chances*</a></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/11/my-conversation-with-the-excellent-donald-s-lopez-jr.html?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=my-conversation-with-the-excellent-donald-s-lopez-jr\">My Conversation with the excellent Donald S. Lopez Jr.</a></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/11/marked-by-time.html?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=marked-by-time\">*Marked by Time*</a></li></ul> </div>","author":"Tyler Cowen","siteTitle":"Marginal Revolution","siteHash":"242a3a39129b36e0c574c3796ca7ef3cf8af967286c2998fabf7240d1ad52a47","entryHash":"02d575a7f0d791c61d34f787e33689530e118b2eec0b4a1480352e8125eb10ac","category":"Sites"}